          <declname>GEP</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Canonicalize array indices to pointer-size integers. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This helps to simplify the logic of splitting a GEP. For example, if a + b is a pointer-size integer, we have gep base, a + b = gep (gep base, a), b However, this equality may not hold if the size of a + b is smaller than the pointer size, because LLVM conceptually sign-extends GEP indices to pointer size before computing the address (<ulink url="http://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#id181">http://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#id181</ulink>).</para>
<para>This canonicalization is very likely already done in clang and instcombine. Therefore, the program will probably remain the same.</para>
<para>Returns true if the module changes.</para>
<para>Verified in @i32_add in split-gep.ll </para>
        </detaileddescription>
